Hi Gabriella,

 "f.hom.ref" and "f.hom.alt" are calculated in lines 635-338 for the below R script:

https://github.com/green-striped-gecko/dartR/blob/master/R/gl.report.heterozygosity.r

 "f.hom.ref" and "f.hom.alt"  are the frequency of the reference and alternative alleles in each individual. They are not helpful in detecting cross-contaminated individuals because the decision of assigning which allele is the reference allele and which is the alternative allele is most of the time arbitrary (i.e. the reference allele is the most common allele within the sample).

I'll reply with other possible ways to detect cross-contaminated samples tomorrow.

Cheers,
Luis

